{"files":[{"file":"<fixture>","diagnostics":[{"code":"T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE","kind":"type","message":"Ambiguous instance for `C`. The goal `C (Pair Int Int)` matches `impl C (Pair Int b)` and `impl C (Pair a Int)`, and neither is more specific than the other. Overlapping impls are allowed only when one of them is more specific than every other match — make them disjoint, or add an impl more specific than all of them. If one of these is a prelude or imported impl you cannot edit, annotate this expression to a type only one of them matches","range":{"end":{"character":17,"line":19},"start":{"character":16,"line":19}},"severity":1,"source":"medaka"},{"code":"W-INCOMPARABLE-IMPLS","help":"add an impl at the two heads' common instance so it is more specific than both, or make the two heads disjoint; without one, a goal matching both is rejected as ambiguous once its type is fully determined, and until then silently takes the first-declared impl (see issue 1183)","kind":"warning","message":"Overlapping impls of C: Pair a Int and Pair Int b are not ordered by specificity — neither head is more specific than the other, so a goal matching both has no most-specific impl to pick","range":{"end":{"character":12,"line":15},"start":{"character":8,"line":15}},"severity":2,"source":"medaka"}]}]}
